Close each file in cat -v.
The -v, -e, -t and -A path closed its files only with
FEATURE_CLEAN_UP, so each operand kept a descriptor open. With enough
operands cat ran out of descriptors and failed to open the rest, as
with about 2000 files on Windows. Close every file but stdin, as
bb_cat() does.

---
 coreutils/cat.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/coreutils/cat.c
+++ b/coreutils/cat.c
@@ -157,7 +157,7 @@
 				fputs_stdout(buf);
 			}
 		}
-		if (ENABLE_FEATURE_CLEAN_UP && fd)
+		if (fd != STDIN_FILENO)
 			close(fd);
 	} while (*++argv);
 
